  "id": "Compound::DB00361 - Gene::7280",
  "verbalization": "Vinorelbine is implicated in the interaction with Tubb2a through a series of molecular binding events. The evidence suggests that Vinorelbine binds to Tubb8, which is subsequently bound by Eribulin or Ixabepilone, both of which in turn bind to Tubb2a. This creates a chain of interactions where Vinorelbine indirectly influences Tubb2a through its binding partners. The lowest common ancestors of these interactions—Organic Heterocyclic Compound and Vinca-Domain Binding Agent—highlight the structural and functional similarities among the compounds involved. The presence of multiple binding pathways, including direct and indirect interactions, supports the notion that Vinorelbine may modulate Tubb2a through a complex network of molecular interactions. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering both direct and indirect relationships in understanding the biological role of Vinorelbine in influencing Tubb2a.",
